      "text": "after two days is the feast of the passover, Matt. 26:2 (Mark 14:1; Luke 22:1). we prepare for thee to eat the passover, Matt. 26:17. prepare that thou mayest eat the passover, Mark 14:12. feast of unleavened bread … called the Passover, Luke 22:1. day of unleavened bread, when the passover must be, Luke 22:7. Behold the Lamb of God, which taketh away the sin, John 1:29. looking upon Jesus … he saith, Behold the Lamb of God, John 1:36. in Jerusalem at the passover, John 2:23. passover, a feast of the Jews, was nigh, John 6:4. I should release unto you one at the passover, John 18:39. it was the preparation of the passover, John 19:14. Christ our passover is sacrificed for us, 1 Cor. 5:7. Through faith he kept the passover, Heb. 11:28. blood of Christ, as of a lamb without blemish, 1 Pet. 1:19.",
